	(text "Each buffer circuit is copied from the Radxa Rock 5B v1.45 schematic, sheet 7 (Au5426, same pinout as TI LMK00304).\nStraps as the reference: input 0 selected, HCSL outputs, reference output off. Outputs have 33R in series\nand 49.9R to ground on each leg. Differences from the reference, to check against the buffer datasheet:\n  - two buffers share the one oscillator (the reference has a single buffer);\n  - each regulator is always enabled (the reference switches it from a GPIO);\n  - the zero-ohm links between the regulator and the four supply pins groups are left out;\n  - two outputs of buffer B are unused and left open.\nThe Wi-Fi slot does not use this clock: its reference clock comes from the processor's combo PHY."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
